.TH EZDXF\-BROWSE "1" "May 2024" "" "User Commands"
.B ezdxf\ browse
\(en PyQt DXF structure browser for DXF debugging and curious people
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezdxf\ browse
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-l\ \fILINE ]
.RB [ \-g\ \fIHANDLE ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The browse command opens a DXF structure browser
to investigate the internals of a DXF file
without interpreting the content.
The intended usage is debugging invalid DXF files,
which cannot be loaded by the
.B ezdxf.readfile()
or the
.B ezdxf.recover.readfile()
functions.
.SS "LINE\ NUMBERS"
The low level tag loader ignores DXF comments (group code 999).
If there are comments in the DXF file
the line numbers displayed in the DXF browser are not synchronized,
use the
.BR ezdxf\-strip (1)
command beforehand to remove all comments from the DXF file
in order to keep the line numbers synchronized.
.SS "GUI\ FEATURES"
The tree view on the left shows the outline of the DXF file.
The number in round brackets on the right side of each item shows
the count of structure entities within the structure layer,
the value in angle brackets on the left side is the entity handle.
.P
The right list view shows the entity content as DXF tags.
Structure tags (data type
.BR <ctrl> )
are shown in blue, a double click on a reference handle (datatype
.BR <ref> )
jumps to the referenced entity,
reference handles of non-existent targets are shown in red.
.P
Clicking on the first structure tag in the list opens the DXF
reference provided by Autodesk in the standard web browser.
.SS "AUTO\ RELOAD"
The browser automatically displays a dialog for reloading DXF files
if they have been modified by an external application.
.SS "MENUS\ AND\ SHORTCUTS"
.TP
.B File Menu
.RS +7n
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Open DXF file...
.I Ctrl+O
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Reload DXF file
.I Ctrl+R
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Open in Text Editor
.IR Ctrl+T ,
open the DXF file in the associated text editor
at the current location
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Export DXF Entity...
.IR Ctrl+E ,
export the current DXF entity shown in the list view as text file
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Copy selected DXF Tags to Clipboard
.IR Ctrl+C ,
copy the current selected DXF tags into the clipboard
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Copy DXF Entity to Clipboard
.IR Ctrl+Shift+C ,
copy all DXF tags of the current DXF entity
shown in the list view into the clipboard
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Quit
.I Ctrl+Q
.RE
.TP
.B Navigate Menu
.RS +7n
.IP \(bu 2n
.B Go to Handle...
